  "policy": [
    "Retained v1 definitions keep exact bytes, admission histories and generator/schema bindings; type historical standing does not withdraw ordinary instances.",
    "New candidates already use the native-supported v2 route. Canonical publication requires exact instance disposition and explicit mixed-version registry selection.",
    "Proposed Definition Registry/v2 uses per-entry carrier/schema/generator/admission bindings. Its own registry carrier/contract successor is an additional reviewed artifact contract, not implicitly admitted here.",
    "Explicit v1-to-v2 conversion requires a new exact representation/Definition version under current identity contracts, original-byte lineage and owner/consumer fidelity assessment. Never replace bytes under an existing (definition_id,version).",
    "relation.supersedes is valid in v1 but absent in v2; no automatic rename to successor-of or dropped edge. An explicit meaning-preserving mapping or revised meaning decision is required.",
    "No automatic downgrade: v2-only relations cannot be erased to fit v1.",
    "Carrier admission, ordinary Definition admission, local native commit, canonical repository publication, source selection and runtime activation are distinct."
  ]
